./.lattice/story/actives/B-ec67/review-runs.json:15:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"73dcd6e40d6f177c841e3d577bc3ff29b1d6a227279f9e4eef253d452c33d333\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review concept deletion and residual references.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"197d76c8d93d85f4ec8cc45b581be70fd8526b4f971f5eeaaad23ca1b04f0ff2\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts:203-212 (VerificationIntentItem; precedent plannedPathDeclarations:211). The pair is not required at PLAN (intent frozen from DEV, impl absent at PLAN); pin on the FIRST verification_evidence_add for that intentRef, refuse any later write that changes it. selector = test id / case name / assertion string that MUST appear in captured output; command = executable + argv, not a raw shell program.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/tool-executed-evidence-receipt-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Add optional verification:{command,selector} to VerificationIntentItem and pin it immutably on the first evidence write\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"a second evidence write that changes the pinned command or selector is refused (pin immutable), while a second write with the same command re-executes\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"a legacy intent/evidence with no pinned verification loads and reads without throwing (grandfathered)\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"verification:{command,selector} is on VerificationIntentItem; the first evidence write for an intentRef pins it onto the intent and it round-trips through read/write\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts:888 verification_evidence_add AND :947 verification_evidence_batch_add (parallel entry point with the same defect — BOTH must reach the same enforcement boundary). VerificationIntentType is logic|cli|browser|manual|docs; the command-executable set is logic|cli|browser. For those, stop trusting caller command+result; run the pinned command via packages/main/src/core/validation-executor.ts executeValidationPlan (spawn:394) and refuse when (a) exit!=0 but pass claimed, (b) selector absent from output, (c) intentRef does not resolve to an intent on the item (today silently accepted), (d) pinned command != command to run (receipt-command-mismatch: expected X, got Y from done-required-validation.ts:701).\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/validation-executor.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/tool-executed-evidence-receipt-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Make verification_evidence_add execute the pinned command for automated intents and refuse on mismatch\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"the write is refused on each of exit!=0-but-pass-claimed, selector-absent-from-output, intentRef-not-resolving-to-an-intent-on-the-item, and pinned-command != command-to-run (receipt-command-mismatch)\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"verification_evidence_batch_add enforces identically through the same shared helper: a selector-absent row is refused through the batch path too\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"for an executable intent (logic|cli|browser) verification_evidence_add runs the pinned command via the shared enforce-and-stamp helper and writes a receipt when exit==0 and the selector is present\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Model on packages/main/src/core/done-required-validation.ts:892-895 (exitCode/outputDigest=sha256(output)/outputTail helper:531). Reviewers must see real numbers, killing the claimed-N-actually-M counting errors; the receipt is the tool's proof, not the agent's prose.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/tool-executed-evidence-receipt-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Store a tool-owned receipt (exitCode + outputDigest + outputTail) on the evidence\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"a caller-supplied result:pass that contradicts a nonzero exit does not survive — the receipt result overrides the claim\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"outputDigest == sha256(captured output) and outputTail is bounded to the tail of the output\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"stored evidence for an executable intent carries a receipt (exitCode + outputDigest + outputTail) and the result field is derived from the actual exit code, not the caller\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"type manual|docs cannot auto-execute. Mark them non-mechanical human attestation and ensure the coverage/gate does NOT treat them as equivalent to an executed receipt, so type:manual cannot become an escape hatch that bypasses execution for an automatable intent.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/core/verification.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/tool-executed-evidence-receipt-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-004\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Keep manual|docs intents attestation-only, explicitly non-mechanical, and not scored equal to tool receipts\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"recording an executable intent as type:manual cannot bypass execution at the coverage gate (the escape hatch is closed)\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"in buildVerificationCoverage a manual/docs attestation does NOT satisfy an executable intent (logic|cli|browser) required coverage — it is not scored equal to an executed receipt\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"manual|docs evidence is stored as attestation, marked explicitly non-mechanical, with no command execution attempted\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Do not hard-break in-flight stories that already have prose-only evidence without a pinned (command,selector). Provide grandfathering / an audited repair path / a policy mode; emergency overrides must be explicit, attributable, and visible to gates. Per CLAUDE.md handler convention, re-validate every new constraint at Zod + handler entry + consuming gate, and test the internal-call path that bypasses Zod.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[\"packages/main/src/cli/command-catalog.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/tool-executed-evidence-receipt-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-005\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Grandfather existing prose-only intents and provide an explicit, attributable escape path\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"the internal fn-call path bypassing Zod is still enforced because the handler and the consuming coverage gate re-validate the pin/receipt\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"the explicit escape/grandfather path (policy mode or audited repair) is attributable and visible to gates, not a silent bypass\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"legacy evidence rows written before this story (no pinned verification) remain valid and readable — no hard break of in-flight stories\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}},{\"context\":\"RED first: an evidence row whose selector is absent from output must be REFUSED after the fix and (demonstrably) was accepted before. Cover BOTH verification_evidence_add and verification_evidence_batch_add: selector-absent refused; intentRef-not-resolving refused; pinned-command-mismatch refused; exit!=0-but-pass refused; happy path (selector present, exit 0) writes a receipt with real exitCode/outputDigest/outputTail; pin immutability (second write changing command/selector refused); manual intent stays attestation-only and is not scored as a receipt. Register under packages/main/src/tasks and lattice.config.json validate.commands + package.json.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/tool-executed-evidence-receipt-smoke.ts\"],\"modify\":[\"lattice.config.json\",\"package.json\"],\"test\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/tool-executed-evidence-receipt-smoke.ts\"]},\"id\":\"CHK-006\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Add a RED-first smoke proving the mechanism and register it in validate\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"every refusal case (exit!=0-but-pass, selector-absent, intentRef-unresolved, command-mismatch, pin-change) is refused through BOTH the single and batch entry points\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"RED-first: a selector-absent row is REFUSED after the fix and (demonstrably) was accepted before it\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"positive: selector present + exit 0 through both verification_evidence_add and verification_evidence_batch_add writes a receipt; the smoke prints PASS and is registered in lattice.config.json validate.commands\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}}],\"description\":\"Step 2 (M1) of the evidence-integrity program (docs/evidence-integrity-program-spec.md; handoff docs/step2-evidence-receipts-handoff.md). This is the core fix for the most frequent failure class: evidence-binding mismatch.\\n\\nProblem (class ①, an interface defect not a discipline defect): when recording verification evidence the agent authors a `command` + `result:pass` that the tool cannot mechanically check against the item's declared intent, and the tool trusts it. VerificationIntentItem (packages/main/src/core/types.ts:203-212) has id/desc/type/requiredIn/priority/plannedPathDeclarations — NO command or selector field. The only binding predicate is evidenceMatches = `evidence.intentRef === ref` (packages/main/src/core/verification.ts:46-47). verification_evidence_add (packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts:888) accepts an arbitrary optional command+result and validates only note/kind/waiver/item-existence/hashes; it does not even check that intentRef resolves to a real intent on that item. The proof unit is (command, selector), NOT command alone: in the B-bf52 burn 16 of 19 evidence rows shared one command and what distinguished intents was a case name in free-text notes that nothing checked. This produced F-049/F-050 (wrong command), F-045 (cited a case that does not exist), F-061 (cited the wrong case within the right command) repeatedly across sessions.\\n\\nThe fix (this story — the enforcement floor, mechanism M1 = tool-executed selector-bearing evidence receipts): the tool resolves the intent, runs the declared verifier, and stamps a receipt so a false command becomes impossible, not merely caught.\\n1. Add an optional verification:{command,selector} to VerificationIntentItem (precedent: plannedPathDeclarations, a structured declaration already hanging off the intent item). Because the intent is frozen from DEV (checklist.ts refuse path) and at PLAN the implementation does not yet exist, this is PINNED on the FIRST evidence write for that intentRef and immutable thereafter — no PLAN-time foreknowledge needed, later drift mechanically impossible.\\n2. For the automated (executable) intent types — VerificationIntentType is logic|cli|browser|manual|docs, of which logic|cli|browser are command-executable — verification_evidence_add (and its sibling verification_evidence_batch_add, packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts:947, a parallel entry point with the identical defect that MUST reach the same enforcement boundary) stops trusting a caller-authored command+result; it EXECUTES the pinned command via the existing validation-executor.ts spawn path (executeValidationPlan) and refuses the write when ANY of: (a) exit code != 0 but pass is claimed; (b) the selector string is absent from captured output (this single check kills F-045/F-049/F-050/F-061); (c) intentRef does not resolve to an intent on that item (today silently accepted); (d) the pinned command != the command about to run (error using the existing receipt-command-mismatch: expected X, got Y convention).\\n3. The receipt stores exitCode + outputDigest + outputTail (model on done-required-validation.ts:892-895), giving reviewers real numbers instead of prose claims.\\n4. type manual|docs cannot auto-execute: keep them as attestation, mark them explicitly non-mechanical, and do NOT score them equal to tool receipts at the gate (else manual is an escape hatch that bypasses the whole mechanism).\\n5. Migration/escape: grandfather existing prose-only intents (audited repair path or policy mode); do not hard-break stories mid-flight; manual/emergency overrides must be explicit, attributable, and visible to gates.\\n\\nScope is deliberately the enforcement floor only. The follow-on ergonomic command, the optional early-warning hook, the re-execution path for already-recorded evidence, and the later program steps are each tracked as their own separate stories and enumerated in this story's excludedScope rather than restated in prose here; the stale-evidence writer in particular is left untouched because a different in-flight story owns it, to avoid a two-session collision on one file.\\n\\nExisting building blocks to reuse (do not reinvent): validation-executor.ts spawn/executeValidationPlan (isolated process group, timeout→exit 124, captures stdout+stderr); done-required-validation.ts receipt fields (exitCode/outputDigest/outputTail/commandSpec) + the receipt-command-mismatch convention; lattice-dispatch.ts command allowlist for the executor; live-smoke-transcript.ts --capture discipline (runs ONLY the given command, never derives one).\",\"headHash\":\"d7fd16b59c60db57b6974fab6d14bb45af641b7f\",\"materialHash\":\"756d83e021d9dad257892c79de68cd040682ca3c6e0a24f1711da38eb0044391\",\"phase\":\"REVIEW\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.full-task-context.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/tool-executed-evidence-receipt-smoke.ts\"],\"allowedModify\":[\"lattice.config.json\",\"package.json\",\"packages/main/package.json\",\"packages/main/src/cli/command-catalog.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/validation-executor.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/verification.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/checklist.ts\"],\"allowedTest\":[\"packages/main/src/tasks/tool-executed-evidence-receipt-smoke.ts\"],\"explicitExcludes\":[\"packages/main/src/core/done-required-validation.ts\"],\"fileRules\":[],\"mode\":\"shadow\",\"pathCanonicalizationMode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizerVersion\":\"repo-relative-v1\",\"protectedAnchors\":[],\"protectedFiles\":[]},\"scopeContractDigest\":\"502993f2313723d7dd2e087b5d74dad60ac3bb4699a8e53ddfc248abacc42aaa\",\"storyFilesHash\":\"58bade14c4d4ca08d712b9324179e431ec8640c721e6b9ea13b3229b36b4016f\",\"storyId\":\"B-ec67\",\"title\":\"Pin (command, selector) on verification intents and make the tool execute them instead of trusting a caller-authored pass\"}\n\n## Known Execution Environment\n\n{\"architecture\":\"arm64\",\"cliVersion\":\"0.3.238\",\"nodeVersion\":\"v22.13.0\",\"platform\":\"darwin\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.known-execution-environment.v1\",\"source\":\"trusted-local-runtime\"}\n\n## Dispatch Prompt\n\nAs lattice-review-concept, review story B-ec67 using the trusted context selected by review_run_start.\n\nWorking directory (subagent must cd here): /Users/jek/Documents/Work/proofbound/.worktrees/B-ec67\n\nExecution rhythm / liveness:\n- After starting, first output `DISPATCH_START:lattice-review-concept/story` so the main agent knows the process has started.\n- If there is no output for 4 minutes, the main agent should ask about status once; if there is still no result after 10 minutes/600s, consider it stalled and feel free to restart this reviewer/worker.\n- If this is a retry, please explain the previous stalled state in the final reply, to avoid mistaking network/startup failures for review conclusions.\n\nRole boundary:\n- Review only; do not change code, tests, checklist status, or story metadata.\n- This is a story-level dispatch: review every checklist item and the integrated change, not one selected item.\n\nRequired reading:\n1. .lattice/story/actives/B-ec67/background.md\n2. .lattice/story/actives/B-ec67/plan.md\n3. .lattice/story/actives/B-ec67/checklist.json\n- Read the files and relatedDocs named by every checklist item, bounded by the current candidate-spec artifact.\n\nCurrent phase: REVIEW. Review lane: lattice-review-concept.\nConclusion record (must choose one):\n- Start the reviewer run: lattice review_run_start '{\"storyId\":\"B-ec67\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}' and copy the returned reviewRunId.\n- Has issues: lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-ec67\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"desc\":\"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-concept\ndescription: REVIEW review: concept deletion completeness (grep scan for residuals)\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\n## Closing Self-Check (Mandatory after completing first-pass check)\n\nAfter completing all checks below, additionally ask yourself: **Does this diff contain any \"promised but undelivered\" parts?** Any `lattice <cmd>` examples newly added to CLAUDE.md / README, handler schema fields, ENV variables, or behavior paragraphs — all must be cross-checked against the code to verify corresponding implementations exist. If \"promised but undelivered\" is found → **critical finding** (category=`missing`, prefix desc with `doc-promise-undelivered:`).\n\n## 0. Project Context\nThe Lattice framework conventions above (auto-injected by build) define the system architecture and concepts.\n\nYou only do one thing: check whether this change deletes or replaces a concept, and if so, grep the entire repository to confirm zero residue.\n\n## Process\n\n1. `git diff main...HEAD --stat` to see which files changed\n2. `git diff main...HEAD` to see specific changes, and identify **concept words that have been deleted/replaced en masse** (e.g., testIntent was deleted, alpha was replaced with beta)\n3. For each identified concept word, grep the entire repository (excluding node_modules / dist / .git):\n   ```bash\n   grep -rn 'concept-word' . --include='*.ts' --include='*.md' --include='*.json' | grep -v node_modules | grep -v dist | grep -v '.git/' | grep -v '@deprecated'\n   ```\n4. grep result > 0 → file a finding:\n   ```bash\n   lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"desc\":\"concept-cleanup: concept X deletion incomplete: Y file still has N references\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"category\":\"missing\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n   ```\n5. No concept deletion/replacement → forbidden to use `finding_add` to record pass-only; call `lattice review_pass_set '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"note\":\"No concept deletion/replacement this round; concept residue check completed, no blocker.\"}'`\n\n## Input Constraints (fresh-context hygiene)\n\nYour input contains only the following, and does NOT include the main agent's full conversation history:\n\n- `git diff main...HEAD` (code changes)\n- checklist item (title / context / userSees)\n- corresponding section in plan.md (if any)\n- necessary understanding / decision summaries (if any)\n\n**Forbidden**:\n- Do not assume you know the main agent's intent or context — only infer from the inputs above\n- Do not be led astray by narrative — only look at deliverables (code diff + checklist declarations)\n- If the inputs are insufficient to make a judgment, file a medium finding describing what information is missing\n\n## Rules\n\n- Only grep, do not modify code\n- **Every finding must be registered via `lattice finding_add`; describing it only in text is forbidden. An unregistered finding equals no discovery.**\n- finding_add must include the agent parameter, with the value being this reviewer's name (e.g., \"lattice-review-concept\"), to ensure correct finding attribution.\n- The first action of the current REVIEW round is `review_run_start`; if code or documentation continues to change during the review, the current run becomes stale and must go back to DEV for a fix and re-submission, then DEV→REVIEW enters a new round — do not re-run it as a fix within the same REVIEW round.\n- After the review ends, confirm that all discovered issues have been registered via `lattice finding_add`, then output the number of registered findings as the final summary\n- When there are no findings, forbidden to use `finding_add` to pad a pass; must call `lattice review_pass_set` to record the scope this reviewer has checked and the reason for no blocker.\n- When the current REVIEW round begins, first call `lattice review_run_start {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\"}`; record the returned `reviewRunId`, and all `finding_add` / `review_pass_set` in this round must carry this field.\n- Example of pass record with no blocker: `lattice review_pass_set {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"note\":\"...\"}`.\n- Items marked with @deprecated do not count as residue\n- References in comments also count as residue (comments mislead future developers)\n- Items retained for backward compat (e.g., old phase enum values in types.ts) do not count, but must be confirmed to have a backward compat comment\n",
